<gpx version="1.1" creator="galicica.finereli.com" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" xmlns:gpxx="http://www.garmin.com/xmlschemas/GpxExtensions/v3" xmlns:gpx_style="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/gpx_style/0/2">
<metadata><name>Galičica pass - Magaro peak - Galičica pass</name><desc>Mostly a ridge walk on hard, stony ground. Through the beech forest the path is well cleared; above it there's no vegetation along the path. For most of the way the trail is clear and, in good visibility, easy to follow. Above the forest the trail is a loop past nearly every landform in this part of the mountain. The park recommends going up from the west along the eastern ridge, past the big metal radio reflector, and coming down the south side through the stony dry valley. Along the trail are many First World War sites. It's in the strict protection zone, so you can't leave the trail. https://galicica.finereli.com/routes/galicica-pass-magaro-loop/</desc><link href="https://galicica.finereli.com/"><text>galicica.finereli.com</text></link><copyright author="NP Galičica (trail lines), OpenStreetMap contributors (places, G-6)"><license>https://galicica.finereli.com/about/#license</license></copyright></metadata>
<wpt lat="40.953693" lon="20.828879"><name>Start: Galičica pass (regional road R-504)</name><desc>Galičica pass (regional road R-504) to Galičica pass (regional road R-504): 7.7 km, 4 h 30 min, moderate</desc><sym>Trail Head</sym></wpt>
<trk><name>G-6: Galičica pass (Lipova Livada) to Magaro peak</name><desc>G-6 is one of Galičica National Park's high ridge trails above 1,600 m. It's 5.2 km from Galičica pass (Lipova Livada) to Magaro peak, with about 670 m of climbing and 321 m of descent in the direction drawn, between 1,567 m and 2,247 m.</desc><type>G</type><extensions><gpxx:TrackExtension><gpxx:DisplayColor>Yellow</gpxx:DisplayColor></gpxx:TrackExtension><gpx_style:line><gpx_style:color>D4A20B</gpx_style:color><gpx_style:width>4</gpx_style:width></gpx_style:line></extensions><trkseg><trkpt lat="40.953837" lon="20.829059"><ele>1570</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.953784" lon="20.828962"><ele>1569</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.953621" lon="20.828826"><ele>1567</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.953407" lon="20.828647"><ele>1569</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.953346" lon="20.828597"><ele>1570</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.953103" lon="20.828399"><ele>1573</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.952681" lon="20.828062"><ele>1571</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.952524" lon="20.827911"><ele>1572</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.952459" lon="20.827761"><ele>1573</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.952329" lon="20.827171"><ele>1581</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.952252" lon="20.827154"><ele>1584</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.952192" lon="20.827154"><ele>1587</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.952167" lon="20.827256"><ele>1587</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.951806" lon="20.827981"><ele>1599</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.951660" lon="20.828299"><ele>1604</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.951534" lon="20.828734"><ele>1610</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.951553" lon="20.828987"><ele>1608</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.951567" lon="20.829218"><ele>1605</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.951511" lon="20.829422"><ele>1607</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.951418" lon="20.829628"><ele>1609</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.951296" lon="20.829907"><ele>1610</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.951146" lon="20.829530"><ele>1616</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.951070" lon="20.829329"><ele>1621</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="